Response to the challenge

Short answer: the challenge is largely right. I would not fund Outcome-Informed Remediation Assurance Triage as the single capability. I would replace it with an incident-led study, and keep the triage design on the shelf as a possible later product.

I should also own part of the drift. At each step I accepted a narrowing that made the work easier to validate, and I never tested whether the narrower thing was still the most valuable one. Validatability is a good reason to pick a first experiment. It is a poor reason to pick the strategy.

